{"id":"4696981","name":"Cam Skattebo","team":"NYG","pos":"RB","grp":"RB","num":"44","head":"https://a.espncdn.com/i/headshots/nfl/players/full/4696981.png","age":24,"exp":"2","college":"Arizona State; Sacramento State","draft":["2025","4","105"],"depth":{"pos":"RB","rank":1,"unit":"3WR 1TE","team":"NYG"},"inj":{"status":"Questionable","note":"Skattebo's explosive run put the Giants within field-goal range before he was subbed out for Devin Singletary, who ran up the middle for a 30-yard score to seal the win on the very next play. Though he told Dan Graziano after the game that he \"felt something\" in his hamstring that prompted him to slide down at the end of his run rather than being tackled to the ground, Skattebo doesn't sound like he'll require an MRI and should be ready to play in the Giants' next game Nov. 8 versus the Eagles following a Week 8 bye. After being limited to just six snaps in a Week 6 loss to the Saints following a string of poor outings to begin the campaign, Skattebo stepped back into a lead role out of the backfield in Sunday's victory and delivered his best performance of the season, finishing with 121 total yards and a touchdown on 18 touches.","date":"2026-10-26T14:09Z","detail":"Hamstring"},"next":null,"dvp":null,"news":[{"h":"Giants unlikely to make big RB trade after Tracy injury","d":"The Giants are expected to lean on Cam Skattebo and Devin Singletary with Tyrone Tracy Jr. on injured reserve.","t":"2026-10-28T05:00:38Z"},{"h":"Giants' Cam Skattebo, John Harbaugh object to lowering helmet penalty","d":"Giants coach John Harbaugh and Cam Skattebo took issue with a first-quarter penalty call Sunday against Houston, when the running back was flagged for unnecessary roughness for impermissible helmet contact.","t":"2026-10-26T23:26:18Z"},{"h":"Cam Skattebo & Co. answer John Harbaugh's call, lead Giants to OT win","d":"The Giants' running back group was called out this past week by coach John Harbaugh. They all stepped up Sunday in Houston